The life of the final incarntaion of Dirk the Wizard:

It started out as a very poor game, indeed. All of my items were worthless
except for a blessed scroll of enchant weapon. After using this, my athame
was charged to +3. In the first two rooms, I found a scroll of enchant weapon
in each, making my weapon +5. I gained levels 2, 3, and 4 without any problems,
and decended into the gnomish mines.

My first encounter was a dwarf which fell to my first blow, and to my joy I 
found dwarvish mithril, a hat, a shield, and boots on him. Little did I know
that this would be my only armor for a long time. I found a small assortment
of non-attack wands (polymorph, secret door detect). 

The Town had a co-aligned temple, which I didn't use effectively until the
way back up, where I IDed all my gems, and increased my ac by 5. My cat had 
died, so I replaced him with a dog that I polymorphed into an iron golem. 
I got my first, and only wish before the castle, and got a PYEC. My iron golem
killed the priest while I wasn't looking, so I cleaned the area of anything
useful (major item was a bag of holding), and headed back to the main path. 

around level 10 I encountered an altar, and went about summoning things, and
polymorphing the items they left behind. I got my GoP, BoS, SoR this way. 
I also got many gems, courtosy of a peaceful Umber Hulk. I got to level 21
here, killing the occasional wraith.

Being satisfied with level 21, I did my quest with no difficulty. When I got 
back, I genocided all Ls and ns (I decided aginst genociding Vs or Es [can you?]
because I thought it would be unsporting of me ;). I decided to go searching 
for fort Ludios. on my quest, I lost my previously gained AC by accidentally
killing a guard. I found the fort... I went in with KITTY 4, now a giant mummy.
Kitty died immediately. When I finally found the enterance, I didn't know what
to expect... what I got was 10-20 creatures, all with wands of create mosnter!
(I counted afterwards, there were 7 wands of create monster) I quickly got 
surrounded, and I realized that unless I unburdened myself, I would die. 
So I dropped my bag of holding and ran. I escaped fine... My bag of holding
met a horrible death at the hands of a Gelatinous cube. ARGH! there went all
my gems, candles, and useful toys... I cleaned out the rest of the Fort without
incident. 

Saddened by my loss of the bag, I went back to my altar, and started doing my
thing again. (At one point I noticed my bell was cursed, so I rang it. the 
two wraith corpses were delicious. I think this item might be a bit powerful as
it is. see my earlier notes in rec.games.hack) With a pair of cursed scrolls of
genocide, I made it to level 30. Thus I adventured forth, poor(er... I had the
stuff from the Fort). On my travels downward, I made/killed KITTY 5-8, DOGGIE 
1-4 and OTHER 1-3. On level 19, I found a co-aligned temple. After dropping 
my AC to -24, I allowed my pet to kill the priest. a few polymorphs on the
spellbooks, and I had every spell I could ever need. 

The trip from there was pretty straight foward. near the end, I realized
I didn't have any candles (see a couple paragraphs up), so I wasted a wish
trying to get some, and ended up poly-piling again. 

The rest of the game was a typical run up, and a typical run through the 
endgame, with the exception of the fire plane. 7 Archons attacked me while
I was burdened, relieving me of 3 of my ALOS. When I lost those amulets, I
became unencumbered, and was able to deal with the situation by running, 
wishing for the scrolls mentioned below, and running around while the monsters
followed.

I found no bones piles. 

I didn't die until the end game. (specifically, until fire)

My wishes this game were as follows:
- PYEC
- blessed amulet of life saving
- 10 candles (got 1. bleah)
- blessed horn of plenty (almost died of hunger 2x)
- blessed amulet of life saving
- 2 cursed scrolls of gold detection (while in fire)
- blessed amulet of life saving


